LaunchSafe Agent Firewall for browsers
Copyright 2026 LaunchSafe

This product includes software developed at LaunchSafe (https://launchsafe.com).

The content scanner, the secret and personal-data detectors and the network
predicates are vendored, Apache-2.0, from the LaunchSafe Agent Firewall (src/
at the root of this repository) into src/vendor/firewall/ by
scripts/sync-firewall.mjs, at the commit named in src/vendor/firewall-commit.ts
(files: own.ts, engine/bytes.ts, engine/network.ts, engine/secrets.ts,
engine/pii.ts, engine/content-html.ts, engine/content-lexicon.ts,
engine/content-scan.ts, vendor/agent-safety/signals.ts, and types.ts, which is
an extract holding only the DataKind type). The files are copied unchanged;
each file's header names its source path and commit, and
`node scripts/sync-firewall.mjs --check` verifies the copies.

Through that firewall, portions of the secret-detection patterns, the
data-capture host list and src/vendor/firewall/vendor/agent-safety/signals.ts
come from the LaunchSafe agent-safety package (Apache-2.0); signals.ts keeps
its own upstream header.

Public Suffix List
------------------
src/engine/psl-data.ts embeds a copy of the Public Suffix List
(https://publicsuffix.org/list/, source repository
https://github.com/publicsuffix/list), generated by scripts/gen-psl.mjs from
the pinned commit named in that file. The Public Suffix List is
Copyright the Public Suffix List authors and is licensed under the Mozilla
Public License, version 2.0 (https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/). The list's source
is available at the repository above, at that commit. The copy is changed only
by being reformatted into a TypeScript module (rules split into plain, wildcard
and exception sets, converted to punycode and sorted); its rules are not
modified. That file is the only part of this product under the MPL-2.0; the
rest is Apache-2.0.
